    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0548" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg478"/>

                <head>No. 267.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 30,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 716.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information a
                    copy of a dispatch from Mr. Heap, chargé d’affaires at Constantinople<anchor
                        n="*" xml:id="d267-f1"/> from which it appears <pb facs="0549" n="479"
                        xml:id="pg479"/> that Lord Dufferin, at Mr. Heap’s request, has instructed
                    Colonel Everett, Her Britannic Majesty’s consul at Erzeroum, to give the
                    American missionaries in that vicinity all the assistance they may desire.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to convey to the British Government an expression of the
                    President’s high appreciation of Lord Dufferin’s courtesy in aiding our minister
                    in the protection of American citizens.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
